<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara's reserves rose to 70.15 bln ringgit.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara's reserves rose to 70.15 bln ringgit.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Negara's gold, foreign exchange and other reserves rose to 70.15 billion ringgit as at June 14 against 69.71 billion a fortnight earlier, the Bank said in a statement on Friday.  </p>
<p>The central bank said its total assets and liabilities rose to 96.72 billion ringgit from 96.44 billion two weeks earlier.</p>
<p>(In bln ringgit)  June 14 1997    June 15 1996     May 31 1997</p>
<p>Reserves		 70.15	     67.06	     69.71</p>
<p>Assets		   96.72	     96.28	     96.44</p>
<p>Currency		 22.30	     19.27	     22.21</p>
<p>Govt paper		1.90		3.04		1.81</p>
</text>
